Implemented `transpose(text)` in `transpose.py`.

**Approach:** split input into lines, transpose column-wise (rows → columns). Per the "pad to the left, don't pad to the right" rule: when a row is too short for a column, emit a `' '` only if some row below it has a character in that column, otherwise drop the tail. This preserves every input character while keeping ragged output.

**Verified:** all 12 cases from the official Exercism canonical suite pass (empty, single row/column, simple, first/second line longer, mixed line length, square, rectangle, triangle, jagged triangle), both prompt examples match, and `py_compile` confirms no syntax errors. No test files created or modified.
